{
  "description": "The proposed works at 1–13 Rajgeer Court, Southall are focused on improving the building’s fire safety by remediating sections of the external wall construction identified as containing combustible materials. The scheme involves removing the existing EPS-insulated external wall system and associated combustible elements on the east and south-east elevations, ground floor areas, and undercroft soffits, replacing them with a non-combustible Webertherm XM silicone render system achieving an A2-s1,d0 fire rating while maintaining a similar appearance and colour finish. In addition, cavity closers and fire-stopping measures will be installed to provide full separation between wall systems and reduce the risk of concealed fire spread. These interventions are intended to enhance fire performance, improve compliance with current fire safety standards and FRAEW recommendations, and maintain the overall external appearance of the building.",
